			"type": "text",
			"text": "Gemuendenaspis angusta is a species of arthrodire known from a single specimen found in the Emsian Hunsrück Slate. It is uniquely long and flat, with a head shield length estimated to be 4.5 centimeters. It is the only brachythoracid with a median crest on its median plate. It was often considered a taxon transitional to the Cocoostidae, however this has not been supported recently."
